---
title: "Row Numbers"
enterprise: true
---

The Row Numbers Feature adds a Column that is always present at the start of the grid where each cell of this column will work as a row header.
The following example demonstrates the grid with Row Numbers and no additional configuration.

To enable Row Numbers, set the grid option `rowNumbers = true`.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-options/properties.json" section="miscellaneous" names=["rowNumbers"] /%}

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: true
}
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Numbers" name="row-numbers-default" /%}

## Cell Selection

When the grid is configured with [Cell Selection](./cell-selection/), clicking a Row Number will select all the currently visible cells in the row.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: true,
    cellSelection: true
}
```

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Numbers with Cell Selection" name="row-numbers-cell-selection" /%}

## Row Selection

When the grid is configured with [Row Selection](./row-selection/) and click selection is enabled via `rowSelection.enableClickSelection`, clicking a Row Number selects the row.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: true,
    rowSelection: {
        mode: 'multiRow',
        enableClickSelection: true
    }
}
```

When [Cell Selection](./cell-selection/) is enabled as well, a Row Number click does both: it selects all the cells in the row and the row itself.

### Suppressing Cell Selection Integration

By default, clicking a row number selects a cell range including all the cells in the row. To prevent this behaviour use the `suppressCellSelectionIntegration` option, which leaves only the [Row Selection](./row-selection/) behaviour so that just the row is selected.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: {
        suppressCellSelectionIntegration: true
    },
    cellSelection: true,
    rowSelection: {
        mode: 'multiRow',
        enableClickSelection: true
    }
}
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="RowNumbersOptions" config={ "description": "" } names=["suppressCellSelectionIntegration"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Numbers with Row Selection" name="row-numbers-row-selection" /%}

## Context Menu

Right-clicking a Row Number cell opens the grid [Context Menu](./context-menu/) with the items returned by
`getContextMenuItems`, whether or not [Cell Selection](./cell-selection/) is enabled.

When Cell Selection is integrated with the Row Numbers Column, the right-click also selects the whole row, so that
items such as `Copy` act on the right-clicked row. A right-click on a row that is already part of a selected row range
leaves that selection untouched.

Where the Cell Selection integration is not in use, a Row Number cell holds no data of its own, so its default items,
and the `defaultItems` passed to `getContextMenuItems`, are the row-level items only, such as `Export`. Cell items
such as `Cut`, `Copy` and `Paste` are not included.

The `contextMenuItems` option overrides `getContextMenuItems` for the Row Numbers Column only.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: {
        contextMenuItems: ['copy', 'export']
    },
}
```

## Row Resizing

To allow the Row Numbers feature to resize rows, the `enableRowResizer` property can be used.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: {
        enableRowResizer: true
    },
}
```

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="RowNumbersOptions" config={ "description": "" } names=["enableRowResizer"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Numbers Row Resizer" name="row-numbers-row-resizer" /%}

{% note %}
The Row Resizer feature does not work when columns are configured with [Auto Row Height](./row-height/#auto-row-height).
{% /note %}

### Row Resize Events

The following events are fired when a row resize operation starts and ends.

{% apiDocumentation source="grid-events/events.json" section="rowEvents" names=["rowResizeStarted", "rowResizeEnded"] /%}

## Value Export

By default, when working with exporters such as [CSV Export](./csv-export/) or [Excel Export](./excel-export/), the value of the Row Numbers column is not exported.
This behaviour can be changed by toggling the `exportRowNumbers` of the export params.

```{% frameworkTransform=true %}
const gridOptions = {
    rowNumbers: true,
    cellSelection: {
        enableHeaderHighlight: true,
        handle: { mode: 'fill' },
    },
    defaultCsvExportParams: {
        exportRowNumbers: true,
    },
    defaultExcelExportParams: {
        exportRowNumbers: true,
    },
}
```

### ExportParams

{% interfaceDocumentation interfaceName="ExportParams" config={ "description": "" } names=["exportRowNumbers"] /%}

{% gridExampleRunner title="Row Numbers with Export" name="row-numbers-export" /%}

